# Cline Rules for Resume Workflow Project

## Environment Requirements
- All commands must run within the activated virtual environment (.venv)
- The project should refuse to execute if not in virtual environment
- Python dependencies are installed in the virtual environment only

## File Structure
- Main entry point: scripts/create_resume.py
- Job description: jd.md
- Profile data: profiles/anil/
- Output directories: career/files/md/ and career/files/pdf/

## Execution Rules
1. Always activate virtual environment first: source .venv/bin/activate
2. Run: python3 scripts/create_resume.py
3. The workflow will:
   - Read jd.md to understand job requirements
   - Load profile data from profiles/anil/
   - Generate tailored resume content
   - Validate output quality
   - Save Markdown and PDF files

## Key Files
- jd.md - Job description input (required)
- profiles/anil/ - Source profile data directory
- scripts/create_resume.py - Main orchestration script
- CLAUDE.md - Documentation for Claude Code

## Required Commands
- source .venv/bin/activate
- python3 scripts/create_resume.py